The fords ran loud and red, and we crossed.

But we crossed too slow. The horde's main strength has swung around the Ashspur and cut the road behind us. We cannot go back. We cannot yet go forward. And the drums say they know exactly where we are.

There is one place in these hills a body can hold: the old watch-castle at Grimwatch Ring, a crown of standing stone with mountains at its shoulders. Its well still runs clean. Its walls still remember how to be walls.

Vala has counted the enemy fires. She will not tell me the number, which tells me the number.

One night. Hold the Ring until the mountain horns answer ours — they will come with first light, or they will not come at all.

Muni has already picked his gate to stand in. He looks, for once, almost cheerful.
